Here's a C# function that takes in the prices of a car, clothes, and a book and calculates the total cost of the purchase, while also ensuring that the price of the car is at least double the combined price of the clothes and the book. The initial prices of the items are: Car - $3000, Clothes - $100, Book - $20.

```csharp
public static void CalculateTotalCost(out double totalCost, out double adjustedCarPrice)
{
    double clothesPrice = 100;
    double bookPrice = 20;
    double carPrice = 3000;

    // Check if the car price is at least double the combined price of the clothes and the book
    if (carPrice < 2 * (clothesPrice + bookPrice))
    {
        // Adjust the car price to meet the constraint
        adjustedCarPrice = 2 * (clothesPrice + bookPrice);
    }
    else
    {
        // The car price already meets the constraint, so use it as is
        adjustedCarPrice = carPrice;
    }

    // Calculate the total cost of the purchase
    totalCost = clothesPrice + bookPrice + adjustedCarPrice;
}
```

To use this function, you can call it with the initial prices of the items:

```csharp
double totalCost;
double adjustedCarPrice;
CalculateTotalCost(out totalCost, out adjustedCarPrice);

Console.WriteLine($"Total cost: ${totalCost}");
Console.WriteLine($"Adjusted car price: ${adjustedCarPrice}");
```

This will output the total cost of the purchase and the adjusted car price.

Yes, you can tell if a message has been read in Slack API endpoints when retrieving a message by its ID. Slack provides a `read` property in the message object that indicates whether the message has been read or not. The value of this property is `true` if the message has been read and `false` if it hasn't.

Here's an example of how you can retrieve a message by its ID using the Slack API and check if it has been read:
```javascript
const axios = require('axios');

async function getMessage(messageId) {
  try {
    const response = await axios.get(`https://slack.com/api/channels.history`, {
      params: {
        channel: '#your-channel',
        count: 1,
        message_ts: messageId,
      },
      headers: {
        'Authorization': `Bearer ${process.env.SLACK_TOKEN}`,
      },
    });

    const message = response.data.messages[0];
    return message;
  } catch (error) {
    console.error(error);
    return null;
  }
}

async function main() {
  const messageId = 'your-message-id';
  const message = await getMessage(messageId);

  if (message) {
    console.log(`Message ${messageId} has been read: ${message.read}`);
  } else {
    console.log(`Message ${messageId} not found.`);
  }
}

main();
```
Replace `#your-channel` with the channel where the message was sent and `your-message-id` with the actual message ID you want to retrieve.

